<section class="bsw-definition" aria-labelledby="bsw-definition-heading">
  <div class="bsw-definition__inner">
    <div class="bsw-definition__intro">
      <p class="bsw-definition__eyebrow">The basics</p>
      <h2 id="bsw-definition-heading" class="bsw-definition__heading">
        What is a barbershop website<span class="bsw-definition__period">?</span>
      </h2>

      <p class="bsw-definition__answer">
        A barbershop website is the dedicated online home for your shop. It brings your brand,
        services, team, location, opening hours and booking options together in one place,
        ideally on your own domain. It helps new clients understand what you offer and makes it
        easier for regulars to find you and book again. A good website works clearly on mobile
        and reflects the business behind the chair.
      </p>

      <p class="bsw-definition__support">
        For an independent shop, it is the one place online that is built around your name, your
        standards and your way of welcoming clients.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bsw-definition__contrast">
      <dl class="bsw-definition__concepts">
        <div class="bsw-definition-concept bsw-definition-concept--profile">
          <dt class="bsw-definition-concept__label">A booking profile</dt>
          <dd class="bsw-definition-concept__text">
            A useful place for clients to arrange an appointment.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="bsw-definition-concept bsw-definition-concept--website">
          <dt class="bsw-definition-concept__label">Your barbershop website</dt>
          <dd class="bsw-definition-concept__text">
            A branded home for your identity, team, services, location and booking journey.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <p class="bsw-definition__note">
        Both can be useful, and what each booking platform offers varies. A website gives the shop
        itself a home of its own.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
